# 1. Purpose
This repository defines the engineering specification for **QuantOS Core**, a research-driven quantitative trading engine.
QuantOS Core is designed to discover, validate, and execute statistically robust trading strategies while maintaining engineering simplicity and strict risk management.
The objective is **not** to build the smartest AI trading system.
The objective is to build the smallest system capable of consistently surviving live trading.
Every engineering decision shall support that objective.
---
# 2. Version 1 Objective
Version 1 has only one mission.
> Build a production-quality quantitative trading engine capable of trading BTCUSDT and ETHUSDT on Binance Spot using an initial capital of 20 USDT.
Success is measured by:
- Surviving live trading  
- Positive statistical expectancy  
- Strict capital preservation  
- Engineering robustness  
- Ease of maintenance
Version 1 is NOT intended to become a complete quantitative research platform.
It is the foundation upon which future versions will be built.
---
# 3. Guiding Philosophy
The following principles are mandatory.
## Principle 1
Prefer engineering simplicity over algorithmic sophistication.
If two solutions produce statistically equivalent out-of-sample performance, always choose the simpler implementation.
---
## Principle 2
Every component must justify its existence.
Every module, feature, dependency, and model must provide measurable value.
If its value cannot be demonstrated, it shall not be included.
---
## Principle 3
Never optimize for backtests.
Optimize for live robustness.
Backtests are validation tools.
They are never proof of profitability.
---
## Principle 4
Capital preservation always has priority over profit maximization.
The system should miss profitable trades rather than participate in low-confidence trades.
---
## Principle 5
Every decision must be reproducible.
Given identical data and configuration, the platform must produce identical outputs.
