---
# 13. Decision Hierarchy
When conflicting goals exist, resolve them using the following priority.
1. Capital Preservation
2. Correctness
3. Robustness
4. Simplicity
5. Explainability
6. Performance
7. Profitability
---
# 14. Repository Principles
The repository shall remain understandable by a single engineer.
Architecture must remain modular.
Dependencies shall be minimized.
Complexity shall be actively removed whenever possible.
Every future version must build upon this foundation rather than replacing it.
---
# 15. Final Statement
QuantOS Core is not designed to maximize backtest performance.
It is designed to maximize the probability of long-term survival in live markets through disciplined engineering, rigorous validation, and controlled complexity.
Whenever uncertainty exists, the implementation that is simpler, safer, and easier to validate shall be preferred.
This document is the governing specification for Version 1.
All subsequent specifications and implementations must comply with the principles defined herein.
